{"name":"Ivy Wreath","hex":"#708d76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ivy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several woody, climbing, or trailing evergreen plants of the genus Hedera.","Any similar plant of any genus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivy"},{"term":"wreath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something twisted, intertwined, or curled.","An ornamental circular band made, for example, of plaited flowers and leaves, and used as decoration; a garland or chaplet, especially one given to a victor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of wreathe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hedera","blocks":[{"text":"Hedera, commonly called ivy, is a genus of 12–15 species of evergreen climbing or ground-creeping woody plants in the family Araliaceae, native to Western Europe, Central Europe, Southern Europe, Macaronesia, northwestern Africa and across central-southern Asia east to Japan and Taiwan. Several species are cultivated as climbing ornamentals, and the name ivy especially denotes common ivy, known in North America as \"English ivy\", which is frequently planted to clothe brick walls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Hedera_algeriensis_kz01.jpg/330px-Hedera_algeriensis_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedera","wikidata":"Q26771"},{"title":"Wreath","blocks":[{"text":"A wreath is an assortment of flowers, leaves, fruits, twigs, or various materials that is constructed to form a ring shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Christmas_Wreath_-_geograph.org.uk_-_639554.jpg/330px-Christmas_Wreath_-_geograph.org.uk_-_639554.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wreath","wikidata":"Q1201922"}],"images":[{"srcset